    <string name="diag_explain_route">Connect first. Without a tunnel, all traffic uses your normal network.</string>
    <string name="diag_explain_private_dns">Private DNS is on. Its queries still travel inside the tunnel, but that provider, not your VPN resolver, answers them. Set it to Off or Automatic to use the VPN\'s DNS.</string>
    <string name="diag_explain_ipv6">The tunnel has no IPv6 route. If your network has IPv6, some traffic could bypass the VPN. Reconnect, or use a server with IPv6.</string>
    <string name="diag_explain_webrtc">Browsers can reveal local addresses through WebRTC. Hi VPN cannot see inside browsers; use a WebRTC leak test page and your browser\'s WebRTC settings.</string>

